Chiwetel Ejiofor started his film career by doing something that many would consider as the absolute peak: he made a film with Steven Spielberg .

&#x201C; Amistad &#x201D; was his very first film and, understandably, he was afraid of peaking too soon.

&#x201C;I was definitely worried about it at the time,&#x201D; he said at Torino Film Festival . Related Stories Is ‘I Play Rocky’ Original or Adapted? Stallone’s ‘Rocky’ Origin Story Faces a ‘Barbie’-Style Oscar Dilemma (EXCLUSIVE) ‘He Walked So I Could Run’: ‘Project Hail Mary’ Breakout James Ortiz on Andy Serkis, Becoming Rocky and the Art of Puppetry

&#x201C;You feel that there are stages to how you develop as an actor and the opportunities you get, and you think they might follow a very linear path. But of course, my first film role was with Steven Spielberg. I realized then, very early on, that it&#x2019;s a deeply unpredictable profession. You can either feel disquiet or anxiety about that, or you have to go with it.&#x201D; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

He added: &#x201C;The opportunities can be sporadic or come from different places and angles that you didn&#x2019;t imagine. Part of the challenge, but also the exciting thing about being an actor, is having the capacity and ability to roll with it, to travel on the journey of it and see where it takes you.&#x201D;

The British actor came to Italy to receive the Stella della Mole award for lifetime achievement.

He admitted that, for the longest time, he didn&#x2019;t see himself as a film actor.

&#x201C;Even though I had done the Steven Spielberg film, I still thought of myself primarily as a theater actor. I worked with the National Theatre in Great Britain, in the West End and with many off-West End theater companies,&#x201D; he said. In 2008, he won the Laurence Olivier Award for best actor for "Othello."

It took Stephen Frears&#x2019; thriller &#x201C;Dirty Pretty Things&#x201D; - which screened at Torino Film Festival on Thursday - to finally change his mind. Frears also received an award at the festival this week. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

&#x201C;I think it was around that time when I started to fall in love with film as well, with film acting and the rhythm and poetry of cinema. A lot of that had to do with Stephen Frears and Chris Menges, who was the cinematographer on that film. It became something that I started to pursue.&#x201D;

For a while, he was able to &#x201C;balance the two very well.&#x201D;

&#x201C;It was when I became more involved in writing and directing that it started taking up a lot of my time outside of acting in films. Historically, this would have been the time I spent on stage. I ended up writing or directing my own films.&#x201D;

Ejiofor has directed two feature films: &#x201C;Rob Peace&#x201D; and &#x201C;The Boy Who Harnessed the Wind.&#x201D; But his return to theater is imminent.

&#x201C;It&#x2019;s still something that I&#x2019;m very passionate about. Finding the time to do as much theater as I want can be challenging, but it&#x2019;s something I&#x2019;m in the midst of conversations about.&#x201D;

He hopes to be involved in another theater production later on next year. In the meantime, he&#x2019;s happy to reflect on some of the highlights of his career, which includes Oscar-winning &#x201C; 12 Years a Slave ,&#x201D; directed by Steve McQueen, also shown at the Italian fest.

In the film, he played Solomon Northup, a free black man who was kidnapped in 1841 and sold into slavery in Louisiana.

&#x201C;I hadn&#x2019;t heard of his story at all. When I was sent the script, I was incredibly moved and shocked by it. Then I read Northup&#x2019;s own memoir. I thought it was an extraordinary story, an extraordinary tale,&#x201D; he said before the screening, praising the story that captured a &#x201C;very tragic period of absence of humanity.&#x201D;

&#x201C;It felt very profound to me. I was just deeply moved. Steve McQueen is a phenomenal filmmaker, incredibly passionate, detailed and thorough, with a wonderful vision and cinematic heart. It was incredibly gratifying to see the film being received the way that it was, globally and by the Academy.&#x201D;

He noted: &#x201C;At its heart, it was always a story about human respect and human dignity.&#x201D;

Gerald R. Molen, the Oscar-winning producer who teamed with Steven Spielberg on films including Schindler&#x2019;s List , Jurassic Park and Minority Report , has died. He was 91.

A longtime resident of Bigfork, Montana, Molen died Monday, his great-niece Rachel Lorraine Pullan announced .

Molen first worked with Spielberg as a unit production manager on The Color Purple (1985), after which the filmmaker offered him his first producing gig, as an associate producer on *batteries not included (1987). Related Stories Music Andy Taylor, Duran Duran Guitarist, Dies at 65 Lifestyle Veruschka, Mesmerizing Supermodel of the 1960s and '70s, Dies at 87

After serving as a producer on the Spielberg-directed Hook (1991), Molen was named head of production at Spielberg&#x2019;s Amblin Entertainment, where he shepherded such films as The Flintstones (1994), The Little Rascals (1994), Little Giants (1994), Casper (1995), Twister (1996) and the Spielberg-directed sequel The Lost World: Jurassic Park (1997). blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[620,350],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450],[4,4],[300,251]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

&#x201C;It was the best job in Hollywood,&#x201D; he said in a 2023 interview, &#x201C;because any movie [Spielberg] directed I got to produce, and any movie the company did I got to oversee.&#x201D;

He shared the best picture Oscar for Schindler&#x2019;s List (1993) with Spielberg and Branko Lustig.

Molen&#x2019;s producing credits outside of Spielberg and Amblin included the best picture winner Rain Man (1988), Days of Thunder (1990), The Other Side of Heaven (2001), Just Like Heaven (2005), The Meg (2018) and Meg 2: The Trench (2023).

Gerald Robert Molen was born on Jan. 6, 1935, in Great Falls, Montana. He and his family moved to North Hollywood in 1947, and his parents, Gerald Sr. and Edith, built a cafe across the street from Republic Pictures in Studio City. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[300,250],[300,251],[620,350],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450],[4,4]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

&#x201C;I got to make friends with the studio guards," he said in 2014. &#x201C;They used to take me on the studio lot and take me to a soundstage or the backlot where they were maybe shooting a Western and stuff me down behind a bale of hay or under a wagon. I got it in my blood.&#x201D;

After high school, Molen enlisted in the U.S. Marine Corps; after 10 months in the service, he landed a job as a truck driver hauling furniture at Republic in 1957.

He moved to Universal in 1959, and on Psycho (1960), he doubled for Anthony Perkins as the driver of a car heading to the Bates Motel (director Alfred Hitchcock was in the back seat giving directions).

Molen rose to head of transportation at the studio, and as a transportation coordinator/captain/supervisor, he worked on Escape to Witch Mountain (1975), Bound for Glory (1976), Coming Home (1978), Being There (1979), Ordinary People (1980) and Absence of Malice (1981).

He graduated to unit production manager on such movies as The Postman Always Rings Twice (1981), Tootsie (1982), A Soldier&#x2019;s Story (1984) and the Spielberg-helmed The Color Purple before embarking on his career as a producer.

Molen also had cameos in films including Rain Man , Days of Thunder , Jurassic Park and two other Spielberg-directed features, Amistad (1997) and Catch Me If You Can (2002).

He produced 2016: Obama&#x2019;s America (2012) and Hillary&#x2019;s America: The Secret History of the Democratic Party (2016), two documentaries written and directed by Dinesh D&#x2019;Souza that were critical of Barack Obama and Hilary Clinton. He wrote about the Obama doc in an opinion piece for THR . blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-thr-article-mid-articleX-uid2' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["btf","mid-articleX","mid"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-articleX") .addSize([[300,250],[300,251],[620,350],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450],[4,4]]) .setLazyLoadMultiplier(2) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

In 2014, he sent a letter to 866 Christian and conservative leaders that accused Hollywood of &#x201C;depravity&#x201D; and causing &#x201C;much damage to America.&#x201D;

&#x201C;Throughout my years in Hollywood, I tried to live my life differently and be a part of projects that I would be proud to have my grandchildren watch,&#x201D; he wrote. &#x201C;It hasn&#x2019;t been easy, but I&#x2019;ve at least tried to stand against the tide of depravity that has too often flourished there.&#x201D;

Pat, his wife of nearly 70 years, died in January 2024 at age 86.

